# Repository map

These repositories are separate checkouts, not submodules. A session that needs
more than one must be granted access to the others; paths are configured locally.

| Repo | Owns | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- |
| task-research | Cross-cutting plans, citation store, task analysis | hed-task, nemar-metadata |
| hed-task | Curated task/process vocabulary | - |
| hed-metadata-toolkit | Tooling for reading and validating metadata | - |
| nemar-metadata | Mirrored nemar dataset metadata | - |

<!-- Confirm which of these are actual git repos vs. plain working folders. It
     changes what worktrees, checkpoints, and per-repo auto memory can do. -->

## Which one is authoritative for what

State this explicitly - it's the question that costs the most time when it's
ambiguous.

- **Task/process vocabulary**: `hed-task` is the source of truth. Do not define
  new task terms in `task-research`; propose them for `hed-task` instead.
- **Dataset metadata**: `nemar-metadata` mirrors nemar.org. Treat it as read-only
  downstream of nemar; never hand-edit mirrored records.
- **Citations**: `task-research` owns the merged citation store. Any separate
  working area is staging only.
- **Reusable code**: `hed-metadata-toolkit`. If a helper is being written twice,
  it belongs here.

## Retired / do not extend

- OpenNeuro integration - superseded by nemar. See `.status/decisions.md`.
  Do not add features to it.

